  "Analysis": {
    "Before": "Two static functions in the monolithic API, compiled in three API-consuming TUs; fallback name borrows TU-local static CharString",
    "After": "API -> two-declaration Object/String identity adapter. Implementation includes only own header,Godot Object/String and cstring; no Node,Luau,domain,service,property/value/conversion or implementation headers",
    "Interface": "Owned godot::String GetLuauClassName(Object*); bool IsLuauClass(Object*,const char*). Borrowed live object/query for synchronous call only; caller resolves ObjectID",
    "Bodies": "Exact alias table and inheritance predicate preserved after explicit name/signature/local UTF8 storage adaptations; no duplicate definitions",
    "Rejected": "Whole ClassName/IsA dispatch would include Player/Value callback/concrete-type policy; table-only extraction splits generic policy; borrowed global mutable fallback would introduce cross-TU overwrite coupling",
    "SpecialCases": "PlayerObject and RobloxValue overrides retained; Mouse ClassName remains after unconditional generic ClassName return, preserving existing source ordering rather than asserting an effective override",
    "Registration": "None added; C++ linkage/visibility follows existing build policy; Linux nm -C confirms one ordinary global definition each"
  },
  "StringLifetimeAudit": {
    "Disposition": "No confirmed supported-call UAF, dangling temporary or concurrency defect; no separate defect/fix commit invented",
    "StaticStorage": "Baseline mapped strings are static literals. Fallback uses mutable TU-local static Godot CharString, not std::string/thread_local. CharString copy assignment retains COW data from c.utf8 temporary until next fallback overwrite",
    "ExistingUses": "Only immediate strcmp in gl_isa, Lua ClassName push and invalid-member formatting; no pointer retention in caches/closures/userdata/tasks. Helpers make no Lua call or yield; fullname argument traversal makes no identity lookup",
    "Copies": "Pinned Luau lapi.cpp:669/677 uses lua_pushlstring with luaS_newlstr; lstring.cpp interns/copies bytes. laux.cpp:87 formats error into Lua strings before raising",
    "Godot": "Pinned generated Object get_class/is_class implementations return String/bool. char_string.hpp copy assignment refs COW data; no pointer into destroyed conversion temporary returned by baseline",
    "GCAndReentrancy": "Extension source registers userthread bookkeeping only and no class-lookup userdata destructor. Existing immediate copies remain valid across supported callbacks; retained Lua strings survive repeated accesses,GC observation,destruction and replacement in actual fixtures",
    "NewContract": "Owned Godot String result; named local CharString in IsA; full-expression String/UTF8 temporaries for Lua push/error callers. No shared mutable fallback buffer, no retained native object, no new class cache",
    "Concurrency": "Existing SceneTree/domain callback execution examined; shared domains are not OS threads. No parallel binding dispatch established or invented, and no general threaded Godot/Luau guarantee claimed",
    "Sanitizers": "Not rerun: no native object ownership change or confirmed lifetime fix. Existing GL-017/018 and previous Part/math-closure limitations retained",
